diff --git a/docs/events.md b/docs/events.md
index 5bc2097..ba355d1 100644
--- a/docs/events.md
+++ b/docs/events.md
@@ -23,4 +23,6 @@ A promise cannot be cancelled. When an attempt does not answer within `timeoutMs
 
 A hung attempt must never stop a later attempt from finishing the job. That is what the retry is for.
 
+So the release itself is written to be repeated and to overlap: the warehouse call is made outside the store's critical section (`store.atomically`), and the status check, the status change and the ledger update happen together inside it. The attempt that gets in first releases; every other attempt, redelivery or reconcile run finds the reservation already released and does nothing.
+
 If every attempt fails, the failure goes to the bus's dead letters and the nightly reconcile (see `operations.md`) picks the work up.
